      Material 3 (GM3) static baseline color tokens — the one palette for light and dark.

      Sources (authoritative; do not invent values):
      - Palette RGB and scheme role mappings: AndroidX Compose Material3 generated tokens
        ColorLightTokens / ColorDarkTokens / PaletteTokens (VERSION v0_210):
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/androidx/androidx/androidx-main/compose/material3/material3/src/commonMain/kotlin/androidx/compose/material3/tokens/PaletteTokens.kt
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/androidx/androidx/androidx-main/compose/material3/material3/src/commonMain/kotlin/androidx/compose/material3/tokens/ColorLightTokens.kt
        https://raw.githubusercontent.com/androidx/androidx/androidx-main/compose/material3/material3/src/commonMain/kotlin/androidx/compose/material3/tokens/ColorDarkTokens.kt
      - Role names and baseline scheme overview: https://m3.material.io/styles/color/static/baseline
      - Token catalog cross-check (light sys roles): https://tokencatalog.dev/md3/styles/color/sets/all
      - Messages UI role mapping (FAB / primary emphasis): https://m3.material.io/styles/color/roles
        (Material’s own examples use Messages: FAB and starred → primary / primaryContainer).

      Google Messages is closed-source; public AOSP Messaging is not the Play Store app.
      Exact proprietary Messages APK hexes for custom bubble presets (Blue, etc.) were not
      confirmed from a public Google source — UI jobs below map onto these baseline roles instead.

      Scrim alphas (32% M3 default is too light for lift; keep 60%/70% black):
      scheme.scrim is Neutral0 (#000000) per ColorLightTokens / ColorDarkTokens.
    -->

